module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.StalkIdealSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.EtaleNeighbourhood.ConormalApproximationChart
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.EtaleNeighbourhood.CompletedBaseChangeFibre
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Pushout.SectionsTensorProduct
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.FiniteType.PresentationGenerators

/-!
# The charts of a base change, presented as the quotients Stacks 0CAY compares

Let `p : Y ⟶ T` be a morphism of schemes, let `t ∈ T`, let `b : W ⟶ T` and let `Y_t ↪ Y ×_T W` be
a closed immersion `j` of the fibre over a point `r : Spec κ(t) ⟶ W` of `W` above `t`, as in
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.HasFibreImmersion`. Over an affine open `T₀` of `T`, an affine open
`W₀` of `W` above it containing the image of `r`, and an affine open `U` of `Y` above it, the base
change has the affine chart `V = pr₁⁻¹U ⊓ pr₂⁻¹W₀`, whose ring of sections is `D ⊗_C B` for
`C = Γ(T, T₀)`, `D = Γ(W, W₀)` and `B = Γ(Y, U)`; and the kernel ideal of `j` on that chart is the
ideal that `I = ker(D → κ(t))` generates.

That is the geometric input Stacks 0CAY's chart-by-chart comparison needs. Composed with Stacks
0CAZ's identification of `D ⊗_C B` with the cokernel of the relation matrix of a presentation of
`B` over `C`, it presents the chart ring as `D[x_1, …, x_n] ⧸ R` with the kernel ideal the image of
`I · D[x_1, …, x_n]`, which is exactly a
`Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation` over the ambient ring and ideal that
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.exists_finiteType_coefficients_associatedGraded_equiv` compares
across.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion`: **the fibre is cut out in the
  chart of the base change by the ideal of the point**. The chart of the fibre and the chart of
  the base change form a pushout square of section rings, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isPushout_appLE_of_isPullback_inter` applied to the cartesian
  square `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.isPullback_fibre_of_immersionData`, and the surjective leg
  of a pushout square carries its kernel to the new kernel,
  `Stacks.Flatness.ker_inl_of_isPushout`.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart`: **the chart of the base
  change, presented as a concrete quotient of a polynomial ring over `D`**, with the kernel ideal
  the image of `I · D[x_1, …, x_n]`.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.equiv_restrict_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart`:
  **the presentation of a smaller chart is the restriction of the presentation of a larger one
  along a renaming of the variables**, which is the commutation law of
  `Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentationHom` — and the renaming, unlike a map defined by
  lifting generators, does not mention the structure map `C → D`, so the one map satisfies that
  law for `b` and for `b'` at once.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.chartQuotientPresentationHomOfRename`: the resulting
  `Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentationHom`.
* `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion_fromSpecStalk`: **for the base
  change along `Spec A ⟶ Spec 𝒪_{T,t} ⟶ T`, which is the `b` of Stacks 0CAY, that surjectivity
  hypothesis is automatic.**

## Implementation notes

The surjectivity of `Γ(W, W₀) → κ(t)` is a hypothesis of
`chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion` for a general `b`, and not a consequence of the data of
`HasFibreImmersion` there: that data constrains `r` only to lie over `t`, and a morphism
`Spec κ(t) ⟶ W` over `t` need not hit a point whose residue field is generated by `Γ(W, W₀)` —
for `W = T = Spec ℤ`, `b = 𝟙` and `t` the generic point it does not, `Γ(W, ⊤) → κ(t)` being
`ℤ → ℚ`.

For the `b` of Stacks 0CAY it is not a hypothesis but a theorem, and for *every* `r` that
`HasFibreImmersion` or `HasConormalIso` admits rather than only for the closed point: see
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.surjective_appLE_of_comp_eq_fromSpecResidueField` and
`chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion_fromSpecStalk` below. That `b` factors through
`T.fromSpecStalk t`, which is a monomorphism, so `r ≫ b = T.fromSpecResidueField t` forces the
ring map underlying `r` to be a retraction of `σ` onto the residue map of `𝒪_{T,t}`, hence
surjective; `r` is then the closed point of `Spec A` whenever `A` is local, by
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.base_eq_closedPoint_completedStalk`. The identification of the
ideal `I` with the maximal ideal of `𝒪^∧_{S,s}` is a separate matter, resting on
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.residueField_map_bijective_of_algebraMap`.

The ideal `I` is a parameter rather than literally `ker(Γ(W, W₀) → κ(t))`, so that a caller whose
`D` is a ring isomorphic to `Γ(W, W₀)` — the completed local ring, rather than the sections of its
spectrum — can name the ideal on its own side.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CAY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CAY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CAZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CAZ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TensorProduct

universe u v w

namespace Stacks.ConormalApproximation

variable {T Y W : Scheme.{u}} (p : Y ⟶ T) (t : T) (b : W ⟶ T)
  (r : Spec (CommRingCat.of (T.residueField t)) ⟶ W) (j : p.fiber t ⟶ pullback p b)
  (hr : r ≫ b = T.fromSpecResidueField t)
  (hfst : j ≫ pullback.fst p b = p.fiberι t)
  (hsnd : j ≫ pullback.snd p b = p.fiberToSpecResidueField t ≫ r)

section Chart

variable {T₀ : T.Opens} {W₀ : W.Opens} {U : Y.Opens}
  (hT₀ : IsAffineOpen T₀) (hW₀ : IsAffineOpen W₀) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
  (hW₀T : W₀ ≤ b ⁻¹ᵁ T₀) (hUT : U ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ T₀)
  (hrW : (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of (T.residueField t))).Opens) ≤ r ⁻¹ᵁ W₀)
  (V : (pullback p b).affineOpens)
  (hV : V.1 = pullback.fst p b ⁻¹ᵁ U ⊓ pullback.snd p b ⁻¹ᵁ W₀)

/-- The preimage in the fibre of the chart of the base change is the chart of the fibre cut out by
the same affine open of `Y`. -/
theorem preimage_eq_of_fibreImmersion :
    j ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 = j ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 ⊓ p.fiberToSpecResidueField t ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤ := by
  simp

include hr hfst hsnd hW₀ hrW hV in
/-- **The sections of the chart of the base change and of the corresponding chart of the fibre
form a pushout square of rings.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPushout_appLE_of_isPullback_inter` for the cartesian square
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.isPullback_fibre_of_immersionData`, whose base is the chosen affine
open `W₀` of `W` and whose two other charts are the chart `V` of the base change and the whole of
`Spec κ(t)`. -/
theorem isPushout_chart_of_fibreImmersion :
    IsPushout
      (CommRingCat.ofHom ((pullback.snd p b).appLE W₀ V.1 (chart_le_preimage_right hV)).hom)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (j.appLE V.1 (j ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) le_rfl).hom)
      (CommRingCat.ofHom
        ((p.fiberToSpecResidueField t).appLE ⊤ (j ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) (by simp)).hom) := by
  have hpre : j ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 = j ⁻¹ᵁ V.1 ⊓ p.fiberToSpecResidueField t ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤ :=
    preimage_eq_of_fibreImmersion p t b j V
  have hsq := (isPullback_fibre_of_immersionData p t b r j hr hfst hsnd).flip
  exact isPushout_appLE_of_isPullback_inter hsq hW₀ V.2
    (isAffineOpen_top (Spec (CommRingCat.of (T.residueField t))))
    (chart_le_preimage_right hV) hrW hpre le_rfl (by simp)

include hr hfst hsnd hW₀ hrW hV in
/-- **The fibre is cut out in the chart of the base change by the ideal of the chosen point.** The
kernel ideal of `j` on the chart `V` is the ideal that the kernel of `Γ(W, W₀) → κ(t)` generates
there. For `W = Spec(𝒪^∧_{S,s})` and `r` the closed point this is the statement that `Y_t` is cut
out in the chart of `Y_σ` by the maximal ideal, which is the geometric input of Stacks 0CAY read
on one chart. -/
theorem chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) :
    Stacks.Conormal.chartIdeal j V =
      (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map
        ((pullback.snd p b).appLE W₀ V.1 (chart_le_preimage_right hV)).hom := by
  have hpo := isPushout_chart_of_fibreImmersion p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hW₀ hrW V hV
  have hk := Stacks.Flatness.ker_inl_of_isPushout hpo hsurj
  rw [Stacks.Conormal.chartIdeal, Scheme.Hom.app_eq_appLE]
  exact hk

section Presentation

variable {C D B : Type u} [CommRing C] [CommRing D] [CommRing B] [Algebra C D] [Algebra C B]
  (eC : Γ(T, T₀) ≃+* C) (eD : Γ(W, W₀) ≃+* D) (eB : Γ(Y, U) ≃+* B)
  (hD : ∀ x : Γ(T, T₀), eD ((b.appLE T₀ W₀ hW₀T).hom x) = algebraMap C D (eC x))
  (hB : ∀ x : Γ(T, T₀), eB ((p.appLE T₀ U hUT).hom x) = algebraMap C B (eC x))

include hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW hV eC hD hB in
/-- **The kernel ideal of the fibre on the chart of the base change is the ideal `I` generates in
`D ⊗_C B`.** Composing `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion` with the
identification `AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsTensorEquiv` of the chart ring with `D ⊗_C B`: the
identification carries a section pulled back from `W₀` to `d ⊗ 1`, so it carries the ideal
generated by the image of `I` to the ideal `I` generates in the tensor product. -/
theorem map_chartIdeal_sectionsTensorEquiv (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) :
    (Stacks.Conormal.chartIdeal j V).map
        (sectionsTensorEquiv (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀ hU eC eD eB
            hD hB :
          Γ(pullback p b, V.1) →+* TensorProduct C D B) =
      I.map (algebraMap D (TensorProduct C D B)) := by
  have hleg : (sectionsTensorEquiv (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀ hU eC eD eB
          hD hB : Γ(pullback p b, V.1) →+* TensorProduct C D B).comp
        ((pullback.snd p b).appLE W₀ V.1 (chart_le_preimage_right hV)).hom =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom : D →+* TensorProduct C D B).comp
        (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) :=
    RingHom.ext fun d => sectionsTensorEquiv_appLE_right (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT
      hV hT₀ hW₀ hU eC eD eB hD hB d
  have halg : (algebraMap D (TensorProduct C D B) : D →+* TensorProduct C D B) =
      Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom :=
    RingHom.ext fun d => by simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply]
  rw [chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hW₀ hrW V hV hsurj,
    Ideal.map_map, hleg, ← Ideal.map_map, hI, halg]

include hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW hV eC hD hB in
/-- **The chart of the base change, presented as a concrete quotient of a polynomial ring over
`D`.** Let `P` present `B = Γ(Y, U)` as `C[x_1, …, x_n]/(f_1, …, f_m)` over `C = Γ(T, T₀)`. The
chart `V` of `Y ×_T W` has sections `D ⊗_C B`, hence is the quotient of `D[x_1, …, x_n]` by the
module of relations of the specialised relation matrix, by Stacks 0CAZ; and the kernel ideal of
the fibre on that chart is the image of `I · D[x_1, …, x_n]`.

This is the data `Stacks.Conormal.ChartAssociatedGradedEquiv.ofQuotientPresentation` consumes,
over the very ambient ring and ideal that
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.exists_finiteType_coefficients_associatedGraded_equiv` compares
across. -/
def chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) :
    Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation j V
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D))
      (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) :=
  chartQuotientPresentationOfBaseChange j V P I
    (sectionsTensorEquiv (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀ hU eC eD eB hD hB)
    (map_chartIdeal_sectionsTensorEquiv p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW V hV
      eC eD eB hD hB I hI hsurj)

/-- The identification of the chart ring with the concrete quotient that
`chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart` uses: the sections of the chart are `D ⊗_C B`, and that
is the cokernel of the relation matrix. -/
theorem chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart_equiv {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) :
    (chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW V hV
        eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj).equiv =
      (sectionsTensorEquiv (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀ hU eC eD eB
          hD hB).trans
        (quotRangeEquivTensor D P).symm.toRingEquiv :=
  rfl

/-- The chart ring element presented by the class of `a` is the image of `aeval a` in `D ⊗_C B`
under the inverse of the chart identification. -/
private theorem equiv_symm_mk_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) (a : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) :
    (chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW V hV
          eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj).equiv.symm
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) a) =
      (sectionsTensorEquiv (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀ hU eC eD eB
          hD hB).symm (MvPolynomial.aeval (R := D) (fun i => (1 : D) ⊗ₜ[C] P.val i) a) :=
  rfl

include hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW hV eC hD hB in
/-- **The function on the source chart that a constant of the ambient polynomial ring presents**:
the section of the chart of `W` that `eD` identifies with the constant, pulled back along the
second projection and restricted to the source.

This and `toSourceHom_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart_X` are the only form in which the
map `Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation.toSourceHom` of this presentation can be computed,
and together they determine it, the ambient ring being generated by its constants and its
variables. -/
theorem toSourceHom_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart_C {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) (d : D) :
    (chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW V hV
          eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj).toSourceHom (MvPolynomial.C d) =
      (j.app V.1).hom
        (((pullback.snd p b).appLE W₀ V.1 (chart_le_preimage_right hV)).hom (eD.symm d)) := by
  have hleg := sectionsTensorEquiv_appLE_right (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀
    hU eC eD eB hD hB (eD.symm d)
  rw [eD.apply_symm_apply] at hleg
  rw [Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation.toSourceHom_apply,
    equiv_symm_mk_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T
      hUT hrW V hV eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj, MvPolynomial.aeval_C,
    show (algebraMap D (TensorProduct C D B)) d =
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom : D →+* TensorProduct C D B) d from by
      simp [Algebra.TensorProduct.algebraMap_apply],
    ← hleg, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]

include hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW hV eC hD hB in
/-- **The function on the source chart that a variable of the ambient polynomial ring presents**:
the generator of `Γ(Y, U)` it names, pulled back along the first projection and restricted to the
source. -/
theorem toSourceHom_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart_X {n m : ℕ}
    (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m)) (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom) (i : Fin n) :
    (chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT hrW V hV
          eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj).toSourceHom (MvPolynomial.X i) =
      (j.app V.1).hom
        (((pullback.fst p b).appLE U V.1 (chart_le_preimage_left hV)).hom
          (eB.symm (P.val i))) := by
  have hleg := sectionsTensorEquiv_appLE_left (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀
    hU eC eD eB hD hB (eB.symm (P.val i))
  rw [eB.apply_symm_apply] at hleg
  rw [Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation.toSourceHom_apply,
    equiv_symm_mk_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T
      hUT hrW V hV eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj, MvPolynomial.aeval_X,
    show ((1 : D) ⊗ₜ[C] P.val i : TensorProduct C D B) =
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight.toRingHom : B →+* TensorProduct C D B) (P.val i) from
      rfl,
    ← hleg, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply]

end Presentation

end Chart

section Restriction

variable {T₀ : T.Opens} {W₀ : W.Opens} {U U' : Y.Opens}
  (hT₀ : IsAffineOpen T₀) (hW₀ : IsAffineOpen W₀) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hU' : IsAffineOpen U')
  (hW₀T : W₀ ≤ b ⁻¹ᵁ T₀) (hUT : U ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ T₀) (hU'T : U' ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ T₀)
  (hrW : (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of (T.residueField t))).Opens) ≤ r ⁻¹ᵁ W₀)
  (V V' : (pullback p b).affineOpens)
  (hV : V.1 = pullback.fst p b ⁻¹ᵁ U ⊓ pullback.snd p b ⁻¹ᵁ W₀)
  (hV' : V'.1 = pullback.fst p b ⁻¹ᵁ U' ⊓ pullback.snd p b ⁻¹ᵁ W₀)
  (hUU : U' ≤ U) (hVV : V'.1 ≤ V.1)
  {C D B B' : Type u} [CommRing C] [CommRing D] [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
  [Algebra C D] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C B']
  (eC : Γ(T, T₀) ≃+* C) (eD : Γ(W, W₀) ≃+* D) (eB : Γ(Y, U) ≃+* B) (eB' : Γ(Y, U') ≃+* B')
  (hD : ∀ x : Γ(T, T₀), eD ((b.appLE T₀ W₀ hW₀T).hom x) = algebraMap C D (eC x))
  (hB : ∀ x : Γ(T, T₀), eB ((p.appLE T₀ U hUT).hom x) = algebraMap C B (eC x))
  (hB' : ∀ x : Γ(T, T₀), eB' ((p.appLE T₀ U' hU'T).hom x) = algebraMap C B' (eC x))
  (res : B →ₐ[C] B')
  (hres : ∀ x : Γ(Y, U), res (eB x) = eB' (Y.presheaf.map (homOfLE hUU).op x))

include hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hU' hW₀T hUT hU'T hrW hV hV' hUU hVV eC hD hB hB' res hres in
/-- **The chart presentation of a smaller chart of the base change is the restriction of the chart
presentation of a larger one, along the renaming of the variables.** Let `U' ≤ U` be affine opens
of `Y` over `T₀`, let `P` and `P'` present `Γ(Y, U)` and `Γ(Y, U')` over `C = Γ(T, T₀)`, and let
`ι` name, among the generators of `P'`, the images of the generators of `P` under the restriction
map. Then a class in `D[x_1, …, x_n] ⧸ R` presents, on the smaller chart, the class of its
renaming along `ι`.

This is the `left_commutes` law of `Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentationHom` for the two
nested charts, and *the same* statement with `b'` in place of `b` is its `right_commutes` law:
the ring map `MvPolynomial.rename ι` does not mention the structure map `C → D`, so the one map
serves the two different `C`-algebra structures that `b` and `b'` put on `D`. A map defined
instead by lifting the generators of `P` through `P'` — the obvious alternative — would depend on
that structure map, and no single such map would satisfy both laws.

The two ingredients are the naturality of the chart identification in the chart of `Y`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.sectionsTensorEquiv_naturality`, and the naturality of Stacks 0CAZ's cokernel
identification in a renaming, `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.map_quotRangeEquivTensor_rename`.

The hypothesis on `ι` is satisfiable for any one pair `U' ≤ U`: a presentation of `Γ(Y, U')` whose
variables include the images of the generators of `P` exists by
`Stacks.exists_presentation_val_eq_of_finiteType`, `Γ(Y, U')` being of finite type over the
Noetherian ring `C`. It is a condition on the *pair* of presentations, so a family of
presentations indexed by the charts can satisfy it only for the nested pairs it was chosen for. -/
theorem equiv_restrict_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart
    {n m n' m' : ℕ} (P : Algebra.Presentation C B (Fin n) (Fin m))
    (P' : Algebra.Presentation C B' (Fin n') (Fin m'))
    (ι : Fin n → Fin n') (hι : ∀ i, P'.val (ι i) = res (P.val i))
    (I : Ideal D)
    (hI : (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map (eD : Γ(W, W₀) →+* D) = I)
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom)
    (a : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D) :
    (chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU' hW₀T hU'T hrW
          V' hV' eC eD eB' hD hB' P' I hI hsurj).equiv
        ((pullback p b).presheaf.map (homOfLE hVV).op
          ((chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU hW₀T hUT
              hrW V hV eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj).equiv.symm
            (Ideal.Quotient.mk
              (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P.relation)) a))) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (LinearMap.range (relationMapOfHom (algebraMap C D) P'.relation))
        (MvPolynomial.rename ι a) := by
  have hnat := sectionsTensorEquiv_naturality (IsPullback.of_hasPullback p b) hW₀T hUT hV hT₀ hW₀
    hU eC eD eB hD hB hUU hU'T hU' eB' hB' hV' hVV res hres
  rw [equiv_symm_mk_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart p t b r j hr hfst hsnd hT₀ hW₀ hU
      hW₀T hUT hrW V hV eC eD eB hD hB P I hI hsurj,
    chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart_equiv, RingEquiv.trans_apply, hnat,
    RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply, ← quotRangeEquivTensor_mk,
    map_quotRangeEquivTensor_rename D P P' res ι hι a]
  exact (quotRangeEquivTensor D P').symm_apply_apply _

end Restriction

/-- **A comparison of two nested pairs of chart presentations, from a renaming of the variables.**
The ring map of the two ambient polynomial rings is `MvPolynomial.rename ι`, which carries
`I · D[x_1, …, x_n]` into `I · D[x_1, …, x_{n'}]` because it fixes the constants; the two
commutation laws are the hypotheses, and are what
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.equiv_restrict_chartQuotientPresentationOfPullbackChart` supplies
for the charts of a base change, once on each side. -/
def chartQuotientPresentationHomOfRename {Z X X' : Scheme.{u}} {i : Z ⟶ X} {i' : Z ⟶ X'}
    {V VW : X.affineOpens} {V' VW' : X'.affineOpens} {hWV : VW.1 ≤ V.1} {hWV' : VW'.1 ≤ V'.1}
    {D : Type v} [CommRing D] {I : Ideal D} {n n' : ℕ} (ι : Fin n → Fin n')
    {R R' : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)} {S S' : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin n') D)}
    (pV : Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation i V
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)) R)
    (pV' : Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation i' V'
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)) R')
    (pW : Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation i VW
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n') D)) S)
    (pW' : Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentation i' VW'
      (I.map (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n') D)) S')
    (hleft : ∀ a : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D,
      pW.equiv (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op (pV.equiv.symm (Ideal.Quotient.mk R a))) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk S (MvPolynomial.rename ι a))
    (hright : ∀ a : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D,
      pW'.equiv (X'.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV').op (pV'.equiv.symm (Ideal.Quotient.mk R' a))) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk S' (MvPolynomial.rename ι a)) :
    Stacks.Conormal.ChartQuotientPresentationHom hWV hWV' pV pV' pW pW' where
  hom := (MvPolynomial.rename ι : MvPolynomial (Fin n) D →ₐ[D] MvPolynomial (Fin n') D).toRingHom
  map_ideal := by
    rw [Ideal.map_map,
      show ((MvPolynomial.rename ι :
            MvPolynomial (Fin n) D →ₐ[D] MvPolynomial (Fin n') D).toRingHom.comp
          (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) D)) =
        (MvPolynomial.C : D →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n') D) from
        RingHom.ext fun d => by simp]
  left_commutes := hleft
  right_commutes := hright

/-- **For the base change along the spectrum of a ring receiving a map out of the stalk, the
surjectivity hypothesis of `chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion` is automatic.** Take
`W = Spec A` and `b : Spec A ⟶ T` the morphism a ring map `σ : 𝒪_{T,t} ⟶ A` determines — for
`A = 𝒪^∧_{S,s}` this is the `b` of Stacks 0CAY. Then every `r : Spec κ(t) ⟶ Spec A` over `t`,
hence every `r` that `Stacks.ConormalApproximation.HasFibreImmersion` or
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.HasConormalIso` admits, induces a surjection on sections, by
`Stacks.ConormalApproximation.surjective_appLE_of_comp_eq_fromSpecResidueField`: the condition
`r ≫ b = T.fromSpecResidueField t` already determines the ring map underlying `r` up to the
residue map of `𝒪_{T,t}`, which is surjective. -/
theorem chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion_fromSpecStalk
    {T Y : Scheme.{u}} (p : Y ⟶ T) (t : T) {A : CommRingCat.{u}}
    (σ : T.presheaf.stalk t ⟶ A)
    (r : Spec (CommRingCat.of (T.residueField t)) ⟶ Spec A)
    (j : p.fiber t ⟶ pullback p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t))
    (hr : r ≫ (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t) = T.fromSpecResidueField t)
    (hfst : j ≫ pullback.fst p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t) = p.fiberι t)
    (hsnd : j ≫ pullback.snd p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t) =
      p.fiberToSpecResidueField t ≫ r)
    {W₀ : (Spec A).Opens} {U : Y.Opens} (hW₀ : IsAffineOpen W₀)
    (hrW : (⊤ : (Spec (CommRingCat.of (T.residueField t))).Opens) ≤ r ⁻¹ᵁ W₀)
    (V : (pullback p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t)).affineOpens)
    (hV : V.1 = pullback.fst p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t) ⁻¹ᵁ U ⊓
      pullback.snd p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t) ⁻¹ᵁ W₀) :
    Stacks.Conormal.chartIdeal j V =
      (RingHom.ker (r.appLE W₀ ⊤ hrW).hom).map
        ((pullback.snd p (Spec.map σ ≫ T.fromSpecStalk t)).appLE W₀ V.1
          (chart_le_preimage_right hV)).hom :=
  chartIdeal_eq_of_fibreImmersion p t _ r j hr hfst hsnd hW₀ hrW V hV
    (surjective_appLE_of_comp_eq_fromSpecResidueField t σ r hr W₀ hrW)

end Stacks.ConormalApproximation

end
